  "Question": "Josanna’s test scores to date are \\(90,\\) \\(80,\\) \\(70,\\) \\(60,\\) and \\(85.\\) Her goal is to raise her test average at least \\(3\\) points with her next test. What is the minimum test score she would need to accomplish this goal?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(80 \\)",
    "B": "\\(82 \\)",
    "C": "\\(85 \\)",
    "D": "\\(90 \\)",
    "E": "\\(95 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "An average is the total score divided by the number of tests, so work backward from the desired average to the required total. Josanna's five scores total\n\\[\n90+80+70+60+85=385,\n\\]\nand her current average is \\(385/5=77\\). Raising it by at least \\(3\\) points means reaching an average of at least \\(80\\).\n\nWith six tests, an average of \\(80\\) requires a total of \\(6\\cdot80=480\\). Her next score must therefore be at least\n\\[\n480-385=\\boxed{95}.\n\\]\nA score of \\(95\\) gives exactly the required average, while any smaller score gives a total below \\(480\\). Thus the minimum is \\(95\\), choice E.",
